.TH AVR\-VM\-UPDATE 1 "" "avr 0.7.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-update \- Update a VM's name, TTL, or SSH keys, or rotate its password.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm update
[OPTIONS] VM_ID_OR_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update a VM's name, TTL, or SSH keys, or rotate its password.
.PP
Use avr vm pause, avr vm resume, or avr vm delete for lifecycle changes.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
New display name.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fITEXT\fR
Extend the TTL window from now (e.g. 8h, 7d). Max 7d.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-key\fR \fITEXT\fR
Replace stored SSH public keys (literal or @path). Repeatable. Applies live on a RUNNING VM, otherwise at next resume. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-rotate\-password\fR
Provision a fresh one-time password (returned in the response).
.TP
\fB\-\-egress\-rules\fR \fITEXT\fR
Replace the per-VM egress rules with this JSON array (or @path to a file).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw API response as JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-https\-port\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Replace public HTTPS ports. Repeatable; applies live on a RUNNING VM, otherwise at next start or resume. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-https\-ports\fR
Publish no HTTPS ports. Applies live on a RUNNING VM, otherwise at next start or resume.
